   "caption": {
    "en": "Jagaddhatri Puja 2026 in Chandannagar, near Kolkata: the town whose light artists light up Durga Puja too ✨\n\nChandannagar's light artists build huge illuminated panels and figures, once from small bulbs and now mostly LEDs: scenes from mythology, folk tales, current events and pure fantasy. They are in demand far beyond the town, including for Durga Puja pandals in Kolkata.\n\nJagaddhatri Navami is on Thursday 19 November by Drik Panchang's Kolkata calendar (some calendars say 18 November), and the town celebrates over several days around it. Photos from 2024.\n\nHave you seen Chandannagar's lights? Tell us in the comments 👇",
